notes.notes:
Zen mode now works both on online and offline games. If the host has Zen mode on, the alien infestation and the ship will have its rules, but players that connect to that game will only have more resistant characters if they also have the mode turned on in their machines.
 The end match screen will now show if you’ve played on zen mode;
 The character selection screen also shows if the match will be in Zen mode or not;
 The warning that used to say the Zen mode would be deactivated on online matches have been removed;
 You can now invite players that have more than one roommate at their local lobbies, meaning playing 2 local + 2 local no longer requires matchmaking to work;
 Fixed remapping feature that stopped working after an earlier patch;
 Fixed an issue that caused rooms to reactivate without anyone opening its doors;
 Fixed issue causing navigation problems while using a controller on the settings screen;
 “Fast Delivery” rule for Weekly Challenges no longer removes the flying robots and the pizza from the shop;
 An attempt to fix the issue that happened when you finished a match and went back to the lobby (invisible housemates). Please tell us if it keeps happening with you, this one is particularly hard to test because it is very inconsistent;

Hope you are all having fun with the game and thanks for all the support and patience during these past weeks. All of these fixes were possible thanks to the help of many community members and players that took their time to give us detailed information about them. You all rock :D

Here is a surprise to you all! While fixing a few issues we found out there was a whole pack of fixes that never made it to our live branch, so we compiled them all in this patch just so everyone can play the best version of Out of Space as soon as possible! Hope you all enjoy this unplanned patch and keep on cleaning houses haha.

IMPROVEMENTS

 The floor now only shines if there are no Alien eggs over it;
 Chinese localization has been updated and improved;
 The height required to teleport an item back to the ship due to being lost in space is now higher, to avoid unnecessary teleports;
 The Rug size has been slightly increased to make sure the are no lines of dirt visible on room corners (my OCD is very happy with this);


BALANCE

 Selling food now rewards a proportional value if that food is already partially eaten (and yes, we know.. we’ll miss this too D: );


BUG FIXES


 [COM] Fixed an issue with the progression file that could cause the game to crash if your computer is synced with non-Gregorian calendar dates (like in Thailand, for example);
 [COM] Aliens will no longer become invisible and reaper for no reason whatsoever;
 [COM] Players no longer automatically start sweeping when receiving a mop for the first time;
 Players will no longer respawn walking inside the shower if they previously died walking;
 Spiky Aliens can no longer damage through the doors;
 [COM] Fixed issue that caused the aliens’ stun effect and wings to not be on the right size or state when the players enter rooms;
 [COM] The “needs cleaning” balloons that appear on dirty appliances will now always disappear after the appliance is washed;
 The “denied” balloon now hides properly as well;
 Fixed the issue causing the Recycler’s texture to change by attempting to unbuild it while using;
 [COM] The ventilation shaft can no longer be dirty without any visual indication of that state, especially in online matches;
 The Aliens will not target ventilation shafts anymore;
 [COM] The ventilation shaft now always stops shaking when it is clean (it used to keep on shaking sometimes);
 Fixed issue causing food and trash to be sold by the wrong prices when inside a fridge;
 [COM] Possible fix that should prevent the egg explosion animation to still play even if you washed it a second before it hatches;
 Eggs will no longer play the hatching animation if they are hidden by the fog;
 The restart match confirmation window can no longer be opened multiple times if the player clicked fast enough;
 Highlight no longer flickers when there are enemies nearby;
 Online players will no longer shake their hands while holding objects (this was very subtle, but it happened);


If you want to know more or participate in testing our next project, please join us on our official  Discord Server .

*As usual, items tagged with [COM] were changes based on community reports and feedbacks!

Hi everyone! Here are the patch notes for this update along with a very important message to all of you:

SLOWING THINGS DOWN

When we released this game in early access, we weren’t really sure for how long we would be able to maintain it there. We just knew it had a lot of potential in it and that getting community feedback would definitely guide us to the right direction. Thanks to your support, we had exactly 10 months of early access before finally releasing the game and, even after the release, we still managed to keep updating the game and improving it based on all the insights the community sent. 

It was a total of 27 patches so far, 12 of them bringing major additions and changes to the game. From online multiplayer to house decorations, weekly challenges to robot companions, all this time made Out of Space way bigger and better than what was originally planned. Not to mention the numerous hotfixes released whenever something serious came up lol. Anyway, my point is that it has been a hell of a ride! Thank you for that.

Now we are aiming for another huge goal that requires our attention: taking the game to consoles. This is no easy task, especially with everything that is happening in the world this year, so it is very hard to have any level of certainty regarding this process. Regardless of that, to reduce the chances of delaying the porting any longer than necessary, we will need to slow down our work on the PC/Mac/Linux versions of Out of Space. 

From now on, we will keep up bug reports and suggestions, but updates will be more spaced out than before and will become more focused on fixes too. We are very grateful for the support you’ve given us and we hope to bring you some exciting news soon! Until then, here are all the fixes and improvements from patch v1.1.2.

BETA WITH EXCLUSIVE CONTENT

While we work and wait for the porting process to end, everyone is welcome to play the game with new types of aliens! All you have to do is to go to Out of Space’s properties on Steam, then click on Betas and opt into the beta (no password required). This will grant you access to new alien mutations that will take part on a future update beforehand. Hope you all enjoy them :D

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/33859462/f14440bf3932ee28ce4057fbbeb0f3f2494fb87c.png

IMPROVEMENTS

 [COM] The Watering Bot:

 Will no longer try to clean unreachable players;
 Now avoids going to sinks too far away unless they need to;
 Also gives up on getting buckets that are inside of showers;
 Grabs the closest bucket, regardless if it is full or not;
 [COM] Added an option to choose between US and EU servers for matchmaking (it used to always connect to the one with the lowest ping);
 Now the animation of falling asleep is canceled it another players wakes you up right when you fall;
 [COM] Eggs spawn on doors will now pause for a while if any player has thrown water into that specific door recently; 
 Aliens will now stop their “getting things dirty” animation if they are pushed away from the original targets;
 The Chef/Watering Bots will no longer show the out of energy balloon when they are not going back to base;
 Players can no longer be pushed around by others when using appliances like the Recycler;
 The Mixer’s animation is now better synced with the behaviour time;


BALANCE

 [COM] The game’s difficulty now has a hard cap regarding how much harder it gets if the players take too long to finish a match. This was preventing the difficulty system to work in an impactful way in long matches;
 [COM] The option to buy a battery at the shop was added on “Secret Santa” to avoid locking progression due to RNG;


BUG FIXES

[COM] It is now *very unlikely* that items will get stuck on players during online matches;
 [COM] Items will no longer get stuck on Recyclers or Mixers;
 [COM] Fixed a bug that caused players to instantly fall asleep when using the Exercise Bicycle while playing with Accessibility Mode on;
 [COM] The ventilation shaft no longer spits dirt when they are clean;
 [COM] Fixed the loading issue that caused the tutorial level to use weekly challenge rules and prevented the instructions to work;
 Fixed issue that caused players to exit the Exercise Bicycle immediately after using them; 
 [COM] Aliens will no longer be deactivated as if they were in another room (making them disappear);
 Fixed negative values popping from the money interface on online matches;
 Food prices are now correctly calculated when selling them in a fridge;
 [COM] Pizza can now be recycled;
 Dog beds and robot bases can now be properly washed once they get dirty;
 [COM] Fixed an issue that causes the dog to freeze completely for no apparent reason;
 [COM] The Pumpkin Garden no longer occasionally spawns nothing while “transgenic garden” challenge is active;
 Aliens will no longer get out of stun even with the “stars” effect over their heads;
 Agents other than the player will now pause when a match ends (they used to keep on moving and making sounds);
 [COM] The “”alien stun” sound effect is now better synced with the hit itself and can be played multiple times to improve the hit feedback; 
 [COM] Players will no longer rest while the game is paused on single player matches;
 Fixed an issue that allowed the first room of every ship to deactivate (it is not supposed to);
 [COM] All the players sleeping on the floor during the “uncomfortable floor” challenge now results in game over;
 The 3D audio now works properly on online matches (it used to follow only the host);
 Fixed the "Flying Aliens without wings" issue;
 Players leaving a lobby no longer sets other players ready;


If you want to know more or participate testing features before release, please join us on our official  Discord Server .

