Hi everyone! We are back with yet another patch notes! We continue the effort to reduce the number of bugs and improve the replayability of the game. Here is what the version 0.8.03b14 has for us. As usual, items tagged as [COM] were changed based on community feedback.

TUTORIAL

We didn’t mention the tutorial last sprint because it was still in test phase, although we made it available for you. You know, a test version of a tutorial is still better than no tutorial at all haha. Well, now it is more polished, less susceptible to soft-blocks and with a working flow, in general. 

That sets it in a place where we are comfortable making it obligatory for new players. It only covers the basic you need to know so you can start learning the rest by playing and having a good time. It’s a 1-8 minutes tiny ship with a little bit of storytelling behind it and it should be no trouble for experienced players to rush through, if so they wish. 

FRIEND INVITE

Now the friend invite is fully functional and playing with your friends is way easier than before! After removing that option from the matchmaking menu, we’ve added it back again! And somehow that makes complete sense..

You can now invite anyone you have in your Steam friends list, regardless of the region they are at, and the invite will go straight to the steam chat. The only restrictions are that you both need to be online and visible on Steam and have the exact same version of the game.

COMPEDIUM

We added a screen to show everything you’ve unlocked or can unlock through the achievements in the game. It has descriptions for previously unlocked items and available achievements, but some hidden achievements will only become accessible once the player meets its requirements.

This is meant to help everyone understand better the game mechanics and have a quick way to read more about any given item, as long as it is available in the shop.

EXERCISE BIKE

A new appliance was added to the game! Getting some exercise done on that bicycle grants the players money over time, beyond the obvious health benefits you’d expect from it. Just to be clear, that last one was a joke and you should not buy that item if you want to see a THIC and muscular Beaver. 

BUT in case you do want to see that, our community member CrimsBacon’s got you covered:

https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/4653571/6b442c7b42a48f0e6713822e07c59b4792abb2cc.png

CHANGES AND ENHANCEMENTS


 The game no longer starts with an Armchair, since falling from exhaustion won’t cause a loose state;
 [COM] Improved ship generator that reduces the chances of multiple corridors connected to each other in the same ship;
 Improved syncing of eggs on doors inside of online matches, what prevents conflicts regarding those eggs positions;
 Ventilation Shafts no longer spit dirt as soon as they become dirty, giving time for the players to react and avoid its hazards; 
 Pressing “F” (keyboard) and “up” (controller D-pad) now shows informations of your character in the game, like hunger and fatigue levels;
 Players now only need to press the use button in order to eat food, instead of holding it down;
 Passing out from fatigue or hunger now forces the shop to close, if the passed out player was controlling it;
 [COM] Dogs now have multiple textures and are even cuter than before.


https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/4653571/434d4510c5f630a2150802658b1901610e207393.gif

ÁUDIO



 Added a jingle to the defeat screen;
 New distortion effect for when the music plays on the porch (outside the ship);
 Adaptive music is turned off until we redesign the system that manages it and was replaced by the full layered version of the theme;
 [COM] Several SFXs were redesigned and remixed;


UI


 Subtle text alignment adjustments in “Life Goals Updated” window;
 [COM] New in-game HUD that prints how many rooms are energized in the ship. This should make the goal of the matches clearer. 
 [COM] Chinese, Japanese and Russian fonts were fixed to have no missing characters in the game texts. Player’s nicknames might still get missing characters, especially in Chinese.
 [COM] Button colliders in the interface were resized to reduce misclicks and facilitate mouse navigation;
 [COM] The matchmaking screen now shows the server region of a room once connected to it;
 [COM] Settings now include options to  both toggle V-sync and set a target frame rate, what should allow players to reduce both CPU and GPU usage if so they wish;
 Playing offline no longer displays “Waiting for Players” in the pre-match screen;
